<title>UK: British Energy September sales rise.</title>
<headline>British Energy September sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nuclear electricity producer British Energy Plc said on Thursday total sales to customers in September rose to 5.5 Terawatt hours (TWh) from 4.95 a year ago.</p>
<p>A Terawatt hour is the largest unit of measurement for electricity sales, representing one billion kilowatt hours.</p>
<p>The following table details sales from each power station in TWh. Comparisons are with September 1995:  </p>
<p> Station		    September 96	    September 95</p>
<p> Hinkley Point B	  0.42			0.83</p>
<p> Hunterston B	     0.81			0.83</p>
<p> Dungeness B		0.55			0.18</p>
<p> Heysham 1		  0.59			0.38</p>
<p> Hartlepool		 0.76			0.82</p>
<p> Torness		    0.66			0.42</p>
<p> Heysham 2		  0.93			0.80</p>
<p> Sizewell B		 0.78			0.69</p>
<p> Total			5.50			4.95</p>
<p>British Energy said total sales to customers in the year to date were 31.46 TWh, up from 28.17 TWh a year ago.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
